<title>FRANCE: Euro should be well managed - IMF's Camdessus.</title>
<headline>Euro should be well managed - IMF's Camdessus.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Monetary Fund chief Michel Camdessus said on Tuesday that the euro should be neither weak, nor strong, but well managed and that any talk of creating a weak euro could turn Germans off the single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;The euro should seek to be neither strong nor weak, it should be well managed,&quot; Camdessus told a conference in Paris.</p>
<p>Any discussion of a &quot;competitive devaluation&quot; of the euro was the surest way to provoke &quot;our German friends&quot; to say they wanted nothing to do with it, he added.</p>
</text>
